# Necromancy's "sacrifices it at the beginning of the next cleanup step" is a delayed triggered ability (CR 603.7): it
# triggers as the cleanup step begins but goes on the stack only after the turn-based actions (CR 514.1, 514.3a), so the
# creature it returned is still there as its controller discards down to their hand size. Bot1 casts Necromancy in its own
# draw step, a time a sorcery couldn't have been cast, returning Bot2's Marauding Mako; Bot2's Ancestral Recall leaves Bot1
# with ten cards. Bot1 discards three at cleanup, which triggers the Mako ("whenever you discard one or more cards"), and
# both triggers go on the stack together. Bot1 puts the Mako's on top: it gets three +1/+1 counters, then the sacrifice
# trigger resolves and Bot1, who controls it, sacrifices it to Bot2's graveyard; Necromancy, enchanting nothing, follows it
# to Bot1's graveyard (CR 704.5m).

